<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leonid Kravchuk</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1934–2022</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leonid Kravchuk was a Ukrainian politician who rose through the Communist Party of the Ukrainian SSR and became chairman of its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/verkhovna-rada">Verkhovna Rada</a> in 1990. He oversaw the declaration of independence on 24 August 1991 and was elected the first president of independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a> in December 1991. He signed the Belovezha Accords dissolving the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> and served until 1994.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leonid-kravchuk.jpg" alt="Leonid Kravchuk" width="308" height="411" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Yuriy Ivanov / Юрий Иванов · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Leonid_Kravchuk_(1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
